  "rendered": "The document describes heat treatments applied to the NiTi wire and its vanadium oxide coating, in this order. First, the superelastic NiTi wire was aged at 600 °C[1] for 1 h[2] in a tube furnace under vacuum[3], to activate its superelastic/shape-memory property. Second, after mechanical polishing and vanadium oxide deposition by ALD, the deposited films were annealed at 450 °C[4] for 30 min[5] in a tube furnace open to air[6], to crystallise the coating as V2O5. The ALD deposition itself ran at a reaction temperature of 200 °C[7], which is a process temperature during deposition rather than a separate post-treatment. The document gives no other heat treatment times or temperatures.",
